{
  "name": "Track Amazon prices in Google Sheets and email price-drop alerts with API.SH",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track Amazon prices and get an email when they drop\n\n### How it works\nEvery morning this workflow reads the Amazon products you track from a Google Sheet, fetches each product's current price with the **API.SH** node, and compares it with the price saved on the last run. It writes the new price, the previous price and the change back to the sheet. When a price falls by more than your threshold, or drops under the target price you set for that product, you get one email listing every alert. Products whose lookup fails or that show no price keep their old values, and the sheet's status column says why.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **API.SH** node (nodes panel → search \"API.SH\") and add your API key from [api.sh](https://api.sh) (1,000 free credits a month; one product lookup is 1 credit).\n2. Make a Google Sheet with a tab named **Products** and these headers: `url`, `title`, `target_price`, `last_price`, `previous_price`, `change_percent`, `availability`, `status`, `last_checked`. Add product URLs (and optional target prices).\n3. Paste the sheet URL into both Google Sheets nodes and connect Google Sheets and Gmail.\n4. In **Settings**, set your email, the drop threshold and the ZIP code prices should be checked for.\n\n### Customization\nChange the schedule, send the digest to Slack instead of Gmail, or add `domain` (e.g. `co.uk`) to the API.SH node for other Amazon marketplaces.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "5de1d561-d08c-4391-9f78-eac750f8d3c8",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Load settings and products\nYour alert email, threshold and the products to check.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "537a6fb8-6c30-4650-8b31-209386ecb81b",
